## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA for privacy-policy drift in a multi-tenant, partner‑integrated data plane. Requires data modeling, lifecycle management, API surfaces, observability, and rollout safety.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model including lineage and policy versions
- Region/tenant-aware metrics
- Lifecycle state machine and RCA templates
- Canary rollout and rollback safeguards

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  region: string;
  policyVersion: string;
  evidenceRefs: string[];
  dataLineage: string;
  rootCause?: string;
  correctiveAction?: string;
  containmentStatus: 'detected'|'investigating'|'contained'|'verified'|'closed';
  timestamps: { detected: string; updated?: string; closed?: string };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the canary rollout for a policy upgrade in this scenario?
- What data access controls and retention would you enforce during CAPA investigations?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CAPA design with privacy considerations in data-labeling.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence and lineage
- Cross-tenant lifecycle with SLAs
- API for CAPA creation/update with logs/traces and policy links
- Privacy metrics: exposure window, recurrence rate
- RCA template and canary rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal CAPA type
class CAPARecord {
  constructor(id, evidence, lineage, owners) {
    this.id = id; this.evidence = evidence; this.lineage = lineage; this.owners = owners;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify exposure window in MTTI terms?
- What telemetry would you add to prove recurrence reduction after rollout?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a CAPA program around data governance, cross-region containment, and traceability after a data-leak fault in a deployment.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage and evidence tagging
- Region-aware CAPA lifecycle gates
- REST API design for CAPA management with linked logs/traces
- Regional leakage metrics and false positive handling
- RCA templates and canary rollback for data sinks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal CAPA data model in TypeScript
type CAPA = {
  capa_id: string;
  incident_time: string;
  data_class: string;
  evidence_refs: string[];
  lineage: string;
  owner: string;
  remediation: string;
  status: 'IDENTIFY'|'CONTAIN'|'INVESTIGATE'|'REMEDIATE'|'VERIFY'|'CLOSED';
  RCA_id?: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you integrate with an existing audit log system?
- How would you enforce access controls for CAPA modification?
